Victor Frey was the director of strategy of the [[Org/Hildebrandt Corporation/index|Hildebrandt Corporation]], one of its C-suite and the man who decided where the company put its weight. He dressed to be seen, in cloth shot with gold thread, sequins, diamonds and jewels, and worked the company's marks into everything he wore. He gave the limpest handshake and liked to say that in business or in life, sometimes you have to kick the puppy.

Airframes were his initiative and a large part of why the company grew as it did. He spoke of pressurised cabins and of opening the frames to the public.

He wore a raiment of deep red, near to fire, the mark of a blessing from the [[Heir of the Plague]]. When [[Geography/Færrin/Calaria/Hallia/Hildebrandt Tower|Hildebrandt Tower]] was taken he was found in the vault among the intruders, holding the book they had come for. He did not leave the building alive.
